Flayr Chop patch for JUCE 8.0.16-security (ea77444750de45e036e0279bb0291144bf8e3688).

MP3 decoder, intensity stereo (MP3Decoder::Layer3SideInfo::Info::doIStereo):
for a long block whose last non-zero band is band 21, maxBandl is 22 and the loop
that copies band 20 into band 21 started at sample 576, writing past the 2 x 576
sample buffer into the rest of the decoder object (UBSan: index 576 out of bounds
for type 'float[576]'). JUCE decodes MP3 itself on Windows and Linux, and on macOS
when Core Audio refuses a file; a 21-byte file was enough (found by Flayr Chop's
tests/fuzz/fuzz_sample_load). Same fix as mpg123's for CVE-2017-11126: nothing to
do above band 21.

Applied by CMakeLists.txt via FetchContent PATCH_COMMAND (cmake/ApplyPatch.cmake).

Flayr-Patch-Marker: modules/juce_audio_formats/codecs/juce_MP3AudioFormat.cpp Flayr Chop: maxBandl

diff --git a/modules/juce_audio_formats/codecs/juce_MP3AudioFormat.cpp b/modules/juce_audio_formats/codecs/juce_MP3AudioFormat.cpp
index 79644b061c..27ff783de7 100644
--- a/modules/juce_audio_formats/codecs/juce_MP3AudioFormat.cpp
+++ b/modules/juce_audio_formats/codecs/juce_MP3AudioFormat.cpp
